WEBVTT

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.213
into a narrative of triumph,

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.755
evincing a better self
in response to things that hurt.

00:03:06.493 --> 00:03:10.795
One of the other mothers I interviewed
when I was working on my book

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:13.144
had been raped as an adolescent,

00:03:13.168 --> 00:03:16.080
and had a child following that rape,

00:03:16.183 --> 00:03:19.063
which had thrown away her career plans

00:03:19.087 --> 00:03:22.327
and damaged all
of her emotional relationships.

00:03:23.073 --> 00:03:26.036
But when I met her, she was 50,

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.438
and I said to her,

00:03:27.462 --> 00:03:30.208
"Do you often think
about the man who raped you?"